          model: "A TNC operates in more than one country, linking places through FDI and contracts into a global production network. Through offshoring it builds its own plants abroad - Samsung's smartphone factories in northern Vietnam make the country one of the world's largest phone exporters. Through outsourcing it contracts other firms - Apple designs in California, but assembly is outsourced to Foxconn in Zhengzhou, China. TNCs choose locations for low labour costs, tax incentives and market access, but keep high-value activities (R&D, branding, finance) in core countries, so most value is captured at headquarters. Control is exercised through ownership, contracts, intellectual property and logistics, which means TNC decisions shape which places are 'switched on' to global networks.",
